---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const allDreams = (await getCollection("obsidianPublishedDreams"))
  .map((col) => col.data)
  .sort((a, b) => b.publishedAt.getTime() - a.publishedAt.getTime());
---

<style>
  .tag-link {
    margin-right: 0.4rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
    display: inline-block;
  }
</style>

<Layout pageTitle={"Dreams"}>
  <h1 id="dreams">Dreams</h1>
  <p>
    I have been keeping a dream journal for a while now, and I thought it would be fun to share some of the most interesting
    dreams here! Note that these have received very little to no editing, except for the fact that I've anonimized every sensitive
    name and location. Enter at your own risk!
  </p>

  <p>
    For some of them I provide a brief analysis or commentaries of the things that struck me. My views on dreams align very much
    with that of Jungian phylosophy, but I of course know very little about symbolism. If you have any comments then know they're
    appreciated!
  </p>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <ul class="embedded blog-posts">
      {
        allDreams.map((dream) => (
          <li>
            <span>
              <i>
                <time datetime={dream.publishedAt.toISOString()}>
                  {dream.publishedAt.toLocaleDateString("en-US", {
                    year: "numeric",
                    month: "short",
                    day: "numeric",
                    timeZone: "America/Costa_Rica",
                  })}
                </time>
              </i>
            </span>

            <a href={`/dreams/${dream.slug}`}>{dream.title}</a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
